          {
           "k": "body",
           "v": "\n\n\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. --\u003e\n## Summary by cubic\nFixes scheduler dependency gating so jobs only start after their `needs` are met, and enforces matrix `fail-fast`/`max-parallel`. Adds runner‑compatible wire formats and routes so the official `actions/runner` can run jobs end‑to‑end; includes dogfood CI and an E2E latency harness.\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Scheduler: runs the `needs` DAG, propagates `needs` outputs, evaluates `success()/failure()/cancelled()`, and honors matrix `max-parallel`/`fail-fast`.\n  - Runner server (`aksh-runner-server`): GHES-style registration and AzDO `_apis` lifecycle with RSA‑based encrypted sessions, async long‑poll messaging with acks, cancellations, log ingestion with secret masking, timeline→event-feed projection, local OIDC, and `/runner/server/_apis/...` aliases for runner v2.335.1.\n  - Protocol/parser (`aksh-gha-protocol`, `aksh-gha-parser`, `aksh-gha-expressions`): runner‑tagged `PipelineContextData` and `TaskStep`; `JobPlan.fail_fast`, `max_parallel`, `secrets_inherit`; `RunnerRegistrationRequest.public_key`; hardened expression scanning and status‑function context; activity‑type trigger filters; materialized secret variables; corrected endpoint/repository shapes.\n  - Conformance/tooling (`aksh-conformance`): golden expansion tests and fuzzing; `scripts/e2e-setup.sh`, `scripts/e2e-start.sh`, `.github/workflows/dogfood.yml`, and `autoresearch.sh` latency harness; docs updated with current status and FIPS note.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Corrects dependency gating and promotes pending jobs after completions; delivers cancellation messages; tracks message acknowledgements; returns valid PATCH responses (incl. `lockedUntil`); fixes `requestId` to Int64.\n  - Defaults step `if` to `success()` and supplies a valid JWT‑shaped `SystemVssConnection` token; fixes action input stringification; hardens expression delimiter scanning; fixes trigger glob matching.\n  - Fixes job message shapes: flattens endpoint authorization, uses repository arrays, adds required system context; gates runner APIs with bearer auth.\n\n\u003csup\u003eWritten for commit dc414158abbeb946c02b26d9970b976f5c51c7ec. Summary will update on new commits.\u003c/sup\u003e\n\n\u003ca href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/preloopdev/aksh/pull/2?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. --\u003e\n\n"
          },
